# Docker build context filter. Treat this repo as PUBLIC and the build context as published: nothing secret, local or
# user-specific may enter an image. Note: this filters `docker build` only, never bind mounts (-v) or `docker cp`.
# Docker matches from the context root, so every pattern carries **/ to apply at any depth. If an image needs a file
# excluded here, re-include that exact path with a ! line and say why.

# Secrets and credentials
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/secrets/
**/credentials*.json
**/.npmrc

# Agent and assistant configuration (local permissions, tokens, worktrees, hook state)
**/.claude/
**/.codex/
**/.claude-flow/
**/.swarm/
**/.hive-mind/
**/.playwright-mcp/
**/.handoff/
**/CLAUDE.local.md
**/agentdb.rvf*
**/ruvector.db

# Git metadata (config can hold remote credentials) and local hooks
**/.git/
.githooks/
.gitleaksignore

# Agent data and Xaibo data (real sessions never leave the machine); synthetic fixtures are public
**/*.jsonl
**/*.jsonl.zst
!test/fixtures/synthetic/**/*.jsonl
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-*
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/private
**/exports/
**/spool/

# Caches (incl. disposable agent profiles under .cache/profiles), build output, reports
**/.cache/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/out/
**/release/
**/build/
**/.vite/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/blob-report/
**/graphify-out/
**/*.log

# OS / editors
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
